Debounce delays execution until calls stop for a set period (resets the timer on every call); throttle executes at most once per fixed interval regardless of call frequency.

- Debounce: search-as-you-type autocomplete, resize-end handlers. Fires once, after the burst ends.
- Throttle: scroll or mousemove handlers, API rate limiting. Fires periodically during the burst.
- Pick debounce when you only care about the final state; throttle when you need steady, ongoing updates.

```js
function debounce(fn, delay) {
  let timer;
  return (...args) => {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn(...args), delay);
  };
}

function throttle(fn, interval) {
  let last = 0;
  return (...args) => {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now - last >= interval) {
      last = now;
      fn(...args);
    }
  };
}
```

